    },
    {
      "path": "audience.curriculum.limitation",
      "text": "The listed components total 180 EC, but the prerequisite relationship for the required thesis remains unresolved. This is a supported credit structure rather than a certified complete pathway."
    },
    {
      "path": "audience.componentNotes.y3-electives",
      "text": "24 EC of approved choice, normally 18 EC in period 1 and 6 EC in period 4. Courses outside the programme require approval and must not overlap. Master’s and applied-sciences courses are normally excluded; exceptions for study abroad follow the approved learning agreement. An optional 12 EC internship may replace two 6 EC electives."
    },
    {
      "path": "audience.componentNotes.y3-thesis",
      "text": "Required 12 EC economics research project. The formal entry rule names earlier methods courses whose relationship to the renewed curriculum needs authoritative clarification."
    },
    {
      "path": "audience.componentNotes.y1-academic",
      "text": "Academic and professional skills are compulsory. The linked academic-language test adds no credits. First-year study advice normally requires 42 of 60 EC, with personal circumstances considered."
    },
